 "statement": {
  "status": "present",
  "value": "A unique common line is a string occurring exactly once in lines1 and exactly once in lines2. Recursive patience diff of a segment pair: emit the common prefix and (after the middle) common suffix as \"  line\"; in the middle, find anchors among lines unique within the middle segments (Anchors are the longest chain of unique common lines whose indices increase in both arrays (patience-diff LCS); among longest chains the one whose list of lines1 indices is lexicographically smallest is chosen (inferred deterministic tie-break for the source's \"any\").); with no anchors emit \"- \" for every middle line of lines1 then \"+ \" for every middle line of lines2; otherwise recurse on each gap before/between/after anchors and emit each anchor as \"  line\".",
  "provenance": [
   {
    "repository": "gamma",
    "revision": null,
    "path": "projects/algorithm_solver/catalogue/authored/hack2hire-chunk02-d-20261028-v1/contracts.json",
    "sha256": "9dc06e544b8d452ad77c5a02cf0a5eda67cb3970df7c62f7334e794e995e29ad",
    "selector": "/problems/32/inferred_spec"
   }
  ]
 },
